    entity:pharma-assistant a onto:Entity,
            class:project,
            owl:NamedIndividual,
            skos:Concept ;
        rdfs:label "Pharma Assistant" ;
        fact:business-context "Article/regulation recommendation scenarios agreed for delivery must be supported so that committed Polpharma functionality is delivered alongside ICD-10 work.",
            "Article/regulation recommendation scenarios are part of the agreed delivery scope for Polpharma and must be delivered alongside ICD-10 work, tracked as an explicit backlog item separate from retrieval-optimization experiments.",
            "Backlog must preserve agreed Polpharma delivery priorities (ICD-10, articles/regulations, already committed delivery items) while adding retrieval-optimization stories prioritized after or alongside committed items, and must distinguish immediate delivery work from optimization/experiment work so optimization does not disrupt committed feature delivery.",
            "Business value: faster access to trusted information (HCPs ask questions naturally instead of navigating multiple systems; reduced friction accessing product, medical, educational and promotional content); consistent and traceable communication (source-grounded responses reduce inconsistent messaging, traceability enables review, audit and improvement); data-driven content strategy via conversation analytics (what doctors ask, missing content, answers needing improvement, which eDetailing materials generate engagement); reusable AI platform for future Polpharma AI initiatives (new knowledge sources, therapeutic areas, agentic workflows, richer analytics).",
            "Business value: scalable HCP engagement via 24/7 digital access to approved Polpharma knowledge, complementing physical representative interactions without relying solely on headcount or geography; faster access to trusted product, medical, educational and promotional content through natural-language questions instead of navigating multiple systems; consistent and traceable communication thanks to source-grounded responses enabling review, audit and continuous improvement; data-driven content strategy.",
            "Content filtering of model responses can break entity cleanup for pharmaceutical entities, which in turn can break follow-up questions and downstream tool calls.",
            "Conversation analytics layer capturing conversation topics and user intents, failed or unresolved journeys, feedback signals (thumbs-up/down, comments), source usage and retrieval path, risk flags for answer quality and compliance, potential adverse-event signals where in scope, and technical/cost telemetry from LLM interactions; supports continuous improvement, quality monitoring, content gap detection and prioritization of future development.",
            "Doctors use the assistant to ask about drug strength (dose) and administration instructions (dosage); ambiguity between the two must be handled.",
            "Doctors use the assistant to ask which drugs can be used for a given disease; drug-recommendation scenarios should operate on standardized medical classifications (ICD-10) and deliver reliable answers.",
            "Doctors using the assistant need correct information when asking about drug strength (dose) vs administration instructions (dosage); dosing and contraindications were identified as high-priority areas where mistakes should be avoided.",
            "Doctors using the assistant want questions about basic drug properties routed to the right retrieval path so answers use the most appropriate drug fields instead of overusing Graph retrieval.",
            "Doctors using the assistant want reliable answers to which drugs can be used for a given disease; the scenario was identified as needed for Polpharma delivery.",
            "Doctors using the assistant want reliable contraindication-related answers (which drugs should not be used for a given condition) and filtered, clinically useful answers for drugs for one disease excluding contraindications for another condition.",
            "Doctors using the assistant want to ask which drugs can be used for one disease while excluding drugs contraindicated for another condition, to receive a filtered and clinically useful answer; the product owner wants to know when AI Search is sufficient and when Graph retrieval is needed.",
            "Dosing and contraindications were identified as high-priority areas where mistakes should be avoided; the dose/dosage scenario is included in critical evaluation cases.",
            "Drug availability hints aim to improve the visit experience and prevent patients returning to the doctor because prescribed products could not be bought. Reimbursement rules set by the Ministry of Health change cyclically; doctors face high financial penalties for incorrectly prescribing reimbursed drugs, and keeping up with rules distracts them from their core work. A ready reimbursement justification speeds up work and reduces risk of error and penalty.",
            "End users should not be artificially limited to the first 10 recommended articles/videos when more relevant materials exist, while long lists must remain usable; Polpharma analytics stakeholders need attribution of article clicks from the assistant in their web analytics system.",
            "End users want article and video recommendations that are more relevant than with vector-only or keyword-only search; solution developers want to determine whether vector-only similar-question retrieval is sufficient or whether hybrid search/reranking should be introduced.",
            "End users want the assistant to return all relevant articles and videos above the configured relevance/similarity threshold rather than being artificially limited to the first 10 results; a solution architect wants ICD-10 vs ATC retrieval choice validated so similar questions do not yield inconsistent or confusing results.",
            "Engineering team wants to review and improve intent-detection quality so that user questions are routed to the correct calculator, retrieval path, or dedicated tool.",
            "Engineering team wants to review and improve intent-detection quality so that user questions are routed to the correct calculator, retrieval path, or dedicated tool; acceptance criteria: known intent-detection mistakes collected and analyzed, routing errors involving calculator selection included in the review, scenario descriptions and examples used by the intent detector updated where needed, improved detector evaluated against historical failure cases.",
            "Funkcje historii rozmów mają zapewnić lekarzowi dostęp do wiedzy przydatnej w terapii obecnych pacjentów lub w obrębie specjalizacji oraz pomóc uniknąć pomyłek przy rutynowym zapisywaniu leków po zmianach refundacyjnych.",
            "Polpharma analytics stakeholders want assistant-generated article links to include configurable query parameters so Polpharma's existing web analytics system can attribute article clicks originating from the assistant (WAP).",
            "Polpharma requires additional metrics for assistant behavior monitoring; intermittent DBAP/Farmindex source-system instability may need to be explained to Polpharma; the product UI is in Polish and article/video labels should feel coherent to end users.",
            "Polpharma wants to improve UX and increase user engagement of its polpharmadlaciebie.pl service using modern technologies including artificial intelligence.",
            "Polpharma wants to increase engagement of users of the polpharmadlaciebie.pl service (doctors). A key medical problem is polypharmacy in an ageing society, where finding active ingredients and their potential interactions is time-consuming; support for the doctor's work in this area is seen as valuable. Potential functional requirements were collected during design thinking workshops held on 27.03.2024.",
            "Polpharma, the largest Polish pharmaceutical company, already runs PolpharmaDlaCiebie.pl, a content portal for doctors. WAP extends this ecosystem into an interactive conversational knowledge interface so HCPs no longer need to manually search product databases, articles, calculators, reimbursement data and promotional materials. The strategic ambition is a scalable AI-native channel complementing medical representative interactions, improving access to consistent medical information and generating insight into HCP information needs.",
            "Product team wants positively rated answers to enrich the example base over time, so the system can improve retrieval and few-shot examples based on real successful interactions (automatic feedback loop).",
            "The 'drug for disease' scenario was identified as needed for Polpharma delivery; doctors using the assistant want reliable contraindication-related answers about which drugs should not be used for a given condition.",
            "The delivery team wants to verify whether removing unnecessary Gremlin calls and restructuring reasoning actually improves response time.",
            "Video records from Vimeo need to be joined with CMS (Squiz) data and indexed consistently; frontend integration needs a consistent result structure across streaming and non-streaming endpoints.",
            "WAP extends Polpharma's digital ecosystem from a content portal into an interactive, conversational knowledge interface, so HCPs no longer need to manually search product databases, articles, calculators, reimbursement data and promotional materials. Strategic ambition: a scalable AI-native channel that complements traditional medical representative interactions, improves access to consistent medical information, and generates actionable insight into HCP information needs. Commercial role: digital medical representative and eDetailing assistant.",
            "WAP operates in a medical and pharmaceutical information context, so it must be designed with safety, compliance and auditability from the start (Responsible AI, safety-by-design). Scope boundaries: WAP does not diagnose, replace clinical judgment or independently interpret clinical cases; it provides source-grounded information and access to approved knowledge. Human oversight per EU AI Act: audit trails for prompts, retrieved sources, model outputs and tool calls; review workflows for problematic answers; escalation paths for uncertain or risky content; user-facing disclaimers; monitoring of anomalies, hallucination risk and source gaps; analytics identifying where knowledge or prompts need improvement.",
            "WAP turns Polpharma promotional and educational assets into interactive content rather than static documents, and collects analytics to improve both the assistant and the content ecosystem." ;
        fact:project-engagement-state "Backlog must preserve agreed Polpharma delivery priorities while adding retrieval-optimization work so optimization does not disrupt committed feature delivery." ;
        fact:project-summary "Conversational pharmaceutical knowledge access covering product information and characteristics, active substances, contraindications and adverse reactions, interactions (where data sources are available), reimbursement information, medical articles and educational materials, clinical calculators via integration, and contextual eDetailing materials for selected Polpharma products; also acts as a digital medical representative via eDetailing.",
            "Defining and implementing AI-based features (e.g. drug assistant with drug interactions, dosing, reimbursement info, availability; conversation history with disease/drug extraction and notifications) to improve UX and increase user engagement of the polpharmadlaciebie.pl service.",
            "Primary users: physicians, pharmacists and other healthcare professionals. Primary use case: fast, source-grounded access to pharmaceutical and medical information. Polish-first experience optimized for Polish medical terminology. Channels: web widget / portal integration and standalone web application, depending on deployment scope.",
            "Project to define possibilities of using modern technologies, including AI, to improve UX and increase user engagement of the polpharmadlaciebie.pl service; identified possibilities will be prioritised and the most important functions specified and implemented in the service.",
            "WAP is an AI-powered conversational platform helping healthcare professionals access verified, source-grounded information about medicines, therapeutic areas, medical content, calculators, reimbursement and eDetailing materials, acting as a digital medical and commercial engagement layer for Polpharma integrated with Polpharma-approved knowledge sources.",
            "Wirtualny Asystent Polpharmy is an AI-native knowledge and engagement platform for healthcare professionals, positioned not as a chatbot but as a controlled digital interface between Polpharma's medical knowledge ecosystem and the healthcare professional community." ;
        fact:solution-direction "A dedicated backlog epic is created for the retrieval optimization initiative; stories on dedicated tools, Gremlin fallback, AI Search replacement, buttons/clarifications, latency, and evaluation are linked to it; scattered existing stories are consolidated; the epic reflects the plan discussed in the workshop rather than isolated technical changes.",
            "Add ICD-10 data to the system integrated with the existing update flow for newly added drugs; map disease names or disease groups to ICD-10 codes or relevant ICD-10 groups usable by downstream retrieval tools that search for drugs related to a condition; build a dedicated tool for the 'drug for disease' scenario so answers do not require the LLM to generate Gremlin dynamically.",
            "Add a clarification flow: when entity resolution for a drug or condition is ambiguous, the assistant detects this and asks the user to confirm the intended drug, disease or other entity instead of guessing, then continues with the appropriate retrieval tool; the flow is aligned with the planned 'buttons' / user confirmation mechanism discussed in the workshop.",
            "Add a structured fallback mechanism: unsupported or rare scenarios are handled by an improved fallback node, so dedicated tools cover frequent cases while the system keeps a controlled path for edge cases.",
            "Add additional Langfuse metrics for key assistant behaviors requested by Polpharma: metrics identified and documented, added to Langfuse traces or sessions where appropriate, Langfuse not used as a decisioning/runtime dependency, compatible with existing tracing, inspectable by the team, tested in dev, limitations of Langfuse-based monitoring documented.",
            "Add evaluation of latency impact of retrieval architecture changes: measure latency before and after key retrieval changes, include fallback reasoning node changes and AI Search replacement for scenarios where Graph is unnecessary, and use results to decide whether an architectural change should be kept.",
            "Add handling for entity-cleanup failures caused by content filtering so that pharmaceutical entities do not break follow-up questions or downstream tool calls.",
            "Add negatively rated production questions (extracted or referenced from the feedback source) to the evaluation dataset, including critical categories such as dosage and contraindications, so future model and retrieval changes are tested against known failure cases and the risk of overfitting to a small existing test set is reduced.",
            "Add non-streaming endpoint support for article/video retrieval responses, aligned with the streaming endpoint structure, compatible with frontend expectations, supporting article and video result types, with consistent result-label mapping and without breaking existing streaming behavior.",
            "Add non-streaming endpoint support for article/video retrieval responses: non-streaming response structure aligned with the streaming endpoint where applicable, result fields compatible with frontend expectations, supports article and video result types, tested locally and/or on dev, existing streaming endpoint behavior not broken, result-label mapping handled consistently.",
            "Add semantic model / field descriptions for Graph and Search outputs so the answer-generation agent can correctly interpret coded or abbreviated fields such as flags and status indicators.",
            "Additional metrics required by Polpharma are identified, documented and added to Langfuse traces or sessions where technically appropriate, compatible with existing tracing, tested in dev, inspectable by the team in Langfuse; Langfuse is not used as a decisioning/runtime dependency and limitations of Langfuse-based monitoring are documented.",
            "Analyze Gremlin query patterns: extract and normalize historical Gremlin queries by removing variable values, identify repeated query patterns, flag patterns mapping to simple field lookups or common structured scenarios as candidates for dedicated tools, and select a practical subset of high-value scenarios for implementation.",
            "Analyze historical Gremlin query patterns (extract and normalize queries by removing variable values, identify repeated patterns, flag simple field lookups and common structured scenarios) so that a practical subset of high-value scenarios can be converted into dedicated deterministic tools.",
            "Analyze historical Gremlin query patterns so that frequently used or simple patterns can be converted into dedicated deterministic tools (user story for the engineering team).",
            "Append configurable (not hardcoded) GET/query parameters to article URLs returned by the assistant, managed via platform/admin configuration; preserve original URLs including existing query strings; parameters identify WAP or another agreed source value; no internal click analytics storage unless separately scoped; behavior documented for client analytics alignment.",
            "Article/video result labels returned from CMS are reviewed for language consistency; team agrees whether labels remain in Polish or are translated to English for technical/frontend consistency; agreed convention applied consistently, mapping from CMS labels to frontend labels documented, Polish UI scenarios remain coherent, tests cover article and video result types.",
            "Asystent Leków (drug assistant) providing drug information to doctors: drug-drug interactions, suggested auxiliary questions to ask the patient before prescribing, tests accompanying drug application (before, during, after), key information for the patient (application, expected time to effect, side effects), and drug availability based on the authorised doctor's location.",
            "Automatic feedback loop: identify positively rated answers from user feedback, extract metadata (question, scenario, successful answer pattern), add approved examples to the few-shot/example retrieval base to improve future responses without manual curation of every example.",
            "Automatic feedback loop: positively rated answers identified from user feedback; system extracts metadata (question, scenario, successful answer pattern); approved examples added to the few-shot/example retrieval base to improve future retrieval and responses without manually curating every successful example.",
            "Azure-native deployment aligned with Polpharma's Azure environment and security expectations: separate dev/test/prod environments, Infrastructure-as-Code provisioning, managed identities and Key Vault for secrets, private network patterns where required, observable runtime with traceable LLM interactions, controlled access to data sources and logs, documented APIs for portal or widget integration. Core stack: Azure OpenAI; LangChain/LangGraph orchestration; LiteLLM gateway; Azure AI Search, vector search and graph/Gremlin retrieval; Python API-first backend with web frontend integration; PostgreSQL, Cosmos DB, Redis, ClickHouse data layer; Langfuse, Application Insights, Log Analytics observability; Terraform and Azure DevOps CI/CD.",
            "Azure-native deployment principles: separate dev/test/prod environments, Infrastructure-as-Code for reproducible provisioning, managed identities and Key Vault for secrets, private network patterns where required, observable runtime and traceable LLM interactions, controlled access to data sources and logs, documented APIs for portal or widget integration. Modular growth platform supporting incremental extension via modules: base pharmaceutical knowledge platform, ChPL/product characteristics knowledge base, medical articles, calculators, adverse reactions and contraindications, reimbursement, drug availability (if source access confirmed), treatment guidelines (if approved sources available), eDetailing module and eDetailing administration, analytics and quality monitoring.",
            "Backend returns all article/video results above the configurable similarity threshold instead of hard-capping to 10; the has_more_results / 'more results exist' disclaimer logic is removed or disabled; frontend displays more than 10 results with collapsing, paging, or progressive reveal, tested on dev with representative result sets.",
            "Backlog item: maintain a list of frequent failure modes with targeted instruction snippets, so that the system receives additional guidance only when a known risky scenario is detected (common-error instruction snippets).",
            "Build a combined tool supporting the query pattern 'drug for X that cannot/should not be used with Y', using ICD-10 mapping where relevant and returning a filtered list rather than requiring the LLM to reason over two independent result sets; analyze historical user questions and classify them into qualitative vs quantitative retrieval scenarios.",
            "Build a dedicated drug-interaction retrieval/tool integration: accepts at least two drug/product inputs, retrieves interaction information from the agreed source, interaction questions are routed to the tool, response clearly presents the source's interaction information, handles missing or ambiguous drug names gracefully; tests for two valid drugs, one unknown drug, and ambiguous product name; scope and source-data responsibility documented before implementation.",
            "Clarification flow: the system detects ambiguous entity resolution and, instead of guessing, asks the user to confirm the intended drug, disease or other relevant entity, then continues with the appropriate retrieval tool; aligned with the planned 'buttons' / user confirmation mechanism discussed in the meeting.",
            "Classify historical questions into qualitative vs quantitative/list-style groups, identify which can be answered by AI Search over SmPC/ChPL fields and which require Graph traversal or structured querying, and use the analysis as input for routing design and future dedicated tool selection.",
            "Classify historical user questions into qualitative questions and quantitative/list-style questions; identify which can be answered by AI Search over SmPC/ChPL fields and which require Graph traversal or structured querying; use the analysis as input for routing design and future dedicated tool selection; replace Gremlin retrieval with AI Search for drug-property questions where possible.",
            "Conversational AI assistant grounded in controlled, Polpharma-approved sources; not a diagnostic system; helps physicians and pharmacists navigate approved pharmaceutical knowledge, educational content and product materials while maintaining boundaries around medical claims, citations, compliance and human oversight.",
            "Create a scenario coverage report using historical user questions and/or historical Gremlin usage analysis that identifies scenarios where AI Search should be enough, scenarios where Graph is required, candidates for dedicated tools, and candidates that can remain handled by fallback logic.",
            "Create a scenario coverage report, based on historical user questions and/or historical Gremlin usage analysis, showing how much historical traffic can be handled by AI Search versus Graph; identify scenarios where AI Search is enough, where Graph is required, and candidates for dedicated tools versus fallback logic, to enable evidence-based retrieval optimization decisions.",
            "Current structured LangGraph-style flow; proposed experiment to compare it with a flatter master-agent-plus-tools architecture to assess whether modern reasoning models can reliably select and use specialized tools.",
            "DBAP/Farmindex downtime or intermittent failures are logged with timestamp, context and failed operation (packshot retrieval, Farmindex reload, DBAP request) so source-system failures can be distinguished from application defects and explained to Polpharma; errors caused by source unavailability are not silently ignored; existing retry/error handling is reviewed and documented; no internal workaround unless separately scoped.",
            "Dawkowanie leków: dla leków wymagających obliczenia dawki system wskazuje link do niezbędnego kalkulatora; w interfejsie dialogowym zbiera wymagane parametry wejściowe, dopytuje o brakujące i podaje wyliczoną wartość dawkowania. Sugestia Lingaro: ze względu na ryzyko pomyłki przy odczycie parametrów, przekierować lekarza do kalkulatora z wynikiem i wprowadzonymi parametrami, co umożliwia prostą modyfikację i optyczną weryfikację.",
            "Decompose selected complex medical questions into smaller retrieval operations, combine intermediate results with deterministic tools such as intersection, test on examples where one-shot Gremlin generation is fragile, and base the final answer on retrieved intermediate outputs rather than unsupported LLM inference.",
            "Dedicated tool accepting a condition or ICD-10 input that returns drugs that should not be used in that context, using a predefined Graph query instead of dynamic Gremlin generation by the LLM; intent detection routes contraindication-style questions to the tool; a combined tool for 'drug for disease but not with condition' returns drugs usable for one disease while excluding those contraindicated for another condition.",
            "Dedicated tool accepting a disease or ICD-10 input and returning matching drugs, using a crafted Graph query rather than LLM-generated Gremlin; intent detection routes 'drug for disease' questions to this tool.",
            "Dedicated tool accepting a disease or ICD-10 input and returning matching drugs, using a crafted Graph query rather than LLM-generated Gremlin; intent detection routes 'drug for disease' questions to this tool. A further dedicated tool is planned for the 'drug contraindicated for condition' scenario based on structured retrieval.",
            "Dedicated tools are used for common scenarios where they exist; rare or unsupported scenarios are routed to an improved fallback reasoning node that uses structured output and direct tool-call execution where applicable; the backlog distinguishes scenarios worth dedicated tooling from scenarios left to fallback handling.",
            "Dedicated tools are used for common scenarios where they exist; rare or unsupported scenarios are routed to the fallback reasoning node, which uses improved structured output and direct tool-call execution where applicable; the backlog distinguishes scenarios worth dedicated tooling from those left to fallback handling; a deterministic list-intersection tool is planned to combine results from multiple retrieval steps without hallucination.",
            "Design high-level scenario routing for drug properties: the routing layer detects when a user asks about a drug property, determines which property or field is needed where possible, invokes the AI Search-based drug-property retrieval tool for supported cases, and avoids excessively narrow low-level scenarios when a higher-level scenario is more manageable, so the system answers using the most appropriate drug fields instead of overusing Graph retrieval.",
            "Differentiators vs typical chatbots: dynamic retrieval over controlled pharmaceutical knowledge sources; source-grounded answers with citations and traceability; Polish-first medical language handling; hybrid retrieval combining graph, semantic search and dedicated tools; observable prompts, tool calls, sources and model behavior; modular platform for eDetailing, analytics, calculators and future modules; responsible AI governance.",
            "During indexing, Vimeo videos without transcripts are not indexed as searchable documents; missing-transcript cases are logged, ingestion continues with remaining videos, and the video can be indexed in a subsequent run once a transcript becomes available, supporting gradual upload/transcription availability; logic covered by tests for missing and available transcript cases.",
            "Evaluate via a controlled experiment whether Polish-language prompts improve retrieval and reasoning quality for Polish medical data compared to current (English) prompting, including scenarios where Polish reasoning was suspected to perform better; assess answer quality and token/cost implications; recommend whether to keep English prompts, move selected prompts to Polish, or use a mixed approach.",
            "Evaluate whether Polish prompts improve retrieval and reasoning quality for Polish medical data, so the system can use the language that produces the most reliable answers.",
            "Evaluate whether semantic search or ranking improves few-shot example retrieval so irrelevant examples are less likely to be selected for Gremlin-related prompting; review current vector-search-based retrieval, check cases where superficially similar questions return semantically wrong examples, and recommend whether semantic search/ranking should replace or augment the current approach. Make the fallback reasoning node return concise structured output instead of long prose to reduce context size, latency and downstream failure risk.",
            "Experimentally compare the current structured LangGraph-style flow with a flatter master-agent-plus-tools architecture, where specialized tools are exposed to a higher-level reasoning agent; evaluate on existing project data whether the model chooses appropriate tool paths, comparing quality, latency and controllability. The experiment is exploratory and not the default delivery architecture unless validated.",
            "Extend Postgres product/entity data with BLOZ identifier and is_polpharma flag (with migration/backfill), use BLOZ for DBAP packshot matching, avoid depending on Gremlin/graph for ownership, change Farmindex refresh from daily to weekly (Saturday night, test env first then production), and collect questionable ICD-10 mappings to report to Polpharma as source data quality issues.",
            "Extract questions marked with negative feedback from the feedback source and add them to the evaluation dataset, including critical categories such as dosage and contraindications where present, to reduce the risk of overfitting to a small existing test set.",
            "Fallback reasoning node to return concise, strict structured output instead of long prose (configured via prompting, output schema, token limits or a combination), reducing context size, latency and downstream failure risk; evaluate the new format against examples where longer reasoning output correlated with poorer results; move Gremlin tool-call execution into the reasoning node.",
            "Field values returned from Graph or Search include human-readable field descriptions (semantic model) so the answer-generation step can correctly interpret coded or abbreviated fields such as flags and status indicators; returned data is accompanied by context explaining each relevant field, and raw technical field values are not presented as user-facing medical explanations.",
            "Flattened 'master agent with tools' architecture experiment: existing project data is used as the evaluation basis; specialized tools are exposed to a higher-level reasoning agent; the experiment measures whether the model chooses appropriate tool paths.",
            "For list-style ICD-10 scenarios, use template-based answer composition: a small model or predefined pattern generates a short Polish introduction and the retrieved product list is appended directly, instead of passing the full list as long context to the main LLM; implement a dedicated ATC retrieval tool separate from the ICD-10 tool with routing of ATC vs ICD-10 questions; validate routing so similar questions do not yield inconsistent results.",
            "Graph RAG with hybrid retrieval: graph-based retrieval for relationship-heavy, structured or quantitative scenarios; AI Search / semantic retrieval for content-heavy, qualitative, article-like or document-fragment scenarios; dedicated tools for repeatable business scenarios (disease-to-drug mapping, ICD-10 based interpretation, reimbursement lookup, structured product queries). Reduces dependency on free-form LLM reasoning and improves latency, explainability and control. Every medical or product answer must be traceable to source material (source grounding as core trust mechanism). Polish medical NLP layer for entity recognition, terminology normalization, inflection/synonymy, intent classification and clarification.",
            "Gremlin execution errors are captured and passed back to the component that can correct the query; the system distinguishes syntax-style failures from missing-field-style failures where possible; the correction path is tested against examples where the first generated query fails; the fallback strategy does not blindly skip to a generic fallback when actionable error information is available.",
            "Handle Gremlin execution failures intelligently: capture errors and pass them back to the component that can correct the query, distinguish syntax-style from missing-field-style failures, test the correction path on examples where the first generated query fails, and avoid blindly skipping to a generic fallback when actionable error information is available.",
            "Historia rozmów: system zapisuje jednostki chorobowe oraz leki, o których lekarz poszukiwał informacji; wysyła powiadomienia o nowych terapiach/lekach związanych ze schorzeniem (z przekierowaniem do materiału źródłowego) oraz powiadomienia o zmianach w zasadach refundacji leków, którymi lekarz był zainteresowany.",
            "Human oversight: audit trails for prompts, retrieved sources, model outputs and tool calls; review workflows for problematic answers; escalation paths for uncertain, non-supported or risky content; user-facing disclaimers and scope boundaries; monitoring of anomalies, hallucination risk and source gaps; analytics identifying where knowledge or prompts need improvement. Pharmaceutical AI governance (EMA mindset, though WAP is an HCP-facing knowledge/engagement assistant, not a diagnostic tool): define intended and out-of-scope use, validate source quality and retrieval performance, test with domain experts, document model/data/prompt behavior, monitor post-deployment, controlled release processes. Layered guardrails: PII/patient data detection and masking, prompt injection and jailbreak protection, hallucination detection and source coverage checks, out-of-scope query detection, medical-risk and compliance-risk flags, content filters adapted to pharmaceutical vocabulary without blocking legitimate medicine names, adverse-event detection logic if in scope.",
            "Identify cases where entity cleanup fails because a model response is blocked by content filtering; evaluate whether a model or deployment with lower content filtering is available for the medical/pharmaceutical use case; if not, define a workaround strategy for problematic pharmaceutical entities that preserves the ability to answer follow-up questions where possible.",
            "Identify cases where entity cleanup fails because a model response is blocked by content filtering; evaluate whether a model or deployment with lower content filtering is available for the medical/pharmaceutical use case; if not, define a workaround strategy for problematic pharmaceutical entities that preserves the ability to answer follow-up questions where possible; keep only currently relevant entities in conversation state so previous drugs or conditions do not incorrectly influence later questions.",
            "Identify drug-property questions answerable from indexed SmPC/ChPL fields and retrieve the relevant fields from AI Search instead of generating or executing Gremlin; pass retrieved context with sufficient source information to the answer-generation step; keep Graph retrieval available for scenarios requiring structured traversal; design high-level scenario routing for drug-property questions.",
            "Identify possibilities of using modern technologies including AI, prioritise them, specify the most important functions and implement them in the service; candidate features include Asystent Leków (drug interactions, pre-prescription questions, accompanying tests, key patient information, drug availability and alternatives, reimbursement information, dosing with calculator redirection and dialog interface) and Historia rozmów (extraction of diseases and drugs, notifications about new therapies and reimbursement changes).",
            "Implement a dedicated ATC retrieval tool separate from the ICD-10 retrieval tool that retrieves products for a given ATC class/group; route ATC-related questions to the ATC tool and ICD-10 condition questions to the ICD-10 tool; validate routing with a test set of ICD-10, ATC and ambiguous therapeutic-area queries, document coverage differences (ATC drug-class oriented vs. broader ICD-10 product mappings), adjust routing logic on repeated misclassification, handle ambiguous cases per agreed rules, and document final routing behavior without reducing quality of existing ICD-10 scenarios.",
            "Improve the intent detector by updating its scenario descriptions and examples and evaluating against historical failure cases; add an automatic feedback loop feeding positively rated answers into the example base for retrieval and few-shot prompting.",
            "Ingest Vimeo transcriptions via the Vimeo SDK/API using only the active text track version; detect and update indexed version when the active transcript changes; skip and log videos without transcripts; keep ingestion script compatible with the current article/video indexing pipeline.",
            "Intent/entity detection distinguishes dose from dosage questions; the routing layer retrieves the correct field depending on detected intent; the known English dose/dosage ambiguity is explicitly addressed in prompts, routing rules, or field descriptions; the scenario is included in critical evaluation cases.",
            "Intent/entity detection distinguishes questions about dose from questions about dosage; the routing layer retrieves the correct field depending on detected intent; the known English dose/dosage ambiguity is explicitly addressed in prompts, routing rules, or field descriptions.",
            "Introduce hybrid search for article and video retrieval so recommendations are more relevant than with vector-only or keyword-only search.",
            "Introduce hybrid search for article/video retrieval combining semantic/vector and keyword signals, configurable through existing search settings, keeping similarity threshold and result-count configuration, with retrieval quality compared against the current approach on representative queries, settings documented for future tuning, and controlled rollout for selected retrieval flows if not enabled globally.",
            "Investigate cases where random English or system-like fragments appear in final answers so that user-facing responses remain clean and professional (QA/product team user story).",
            "Investigate cases where random English or system-like fragments appear in final answers so user-facing responses stay clean and professional: collect examples, determine whether the cause is model behavior, prompt leakage, intermediate reasoning leakage, or platform behavior, add the issue to the evaluation dataset or regression checks, and propose a mitigation once the source is identified. A further backlog item is to evaluate Polish prompting for Polish medical retrieval scenarios.",
            "Investigate random English/system-like fragments in final answers: collect examples, check whether the cause is model behavior, prompt leakage, intermediate reasoning leakage, or platform behavior, add the issue to the evaluation dataset or regression checks, and propose a mitigation once the source is identified.",
            "Keep only currently relevant entities in conversation state: review entity state before tool calls, remove or deprioritize irrelevant entities from previous turns, account for follow-up questions where a previously mentioned entity is still relevant, and support dedicated tool calls relying on clean slot filling.",
            "Maintain a list of frequent failure modes, each with a short instruction snippet describing how to handle it, injected as guidance when the corresponding scenario is detected (initial candidates include dose/dosage confusion and other high-frequency testing errors); handle Gremlin execution failures intelligently so syntax or missing-field errors can be used to recover instead of immediately falling back to a less precise path.",
            "Maintain a list of frequent failure modes, each with a short instruction snippet describing how to handle it, so the system can inject relevant guidance only when a known risky scenario is detected; initial candidates include dose/dosage confusion and other high-frequency errors identified during testing. Also planned: a fallback/error-handling strategy for Gremlin execution failures.",
            "Make the question-paraphrasing node generate short, content-focused, system-oriented search queries that preserve medically relevant terms and avoid narrative phrasing such as \"the user asks about...\", so vector search retrieves more relevant few-shot examples; evaluate retrieval quality against cases where vector search previously returned weak examples.",
            "Map Vimeo videos to Squiz/CMS IDs by extracting the CMS ID from the Vimeo description field; handle and log records without required IDs, support partial video availability during uploads, avoid indexing unmatched videos as valid CMS-linked content, cover mapping logic with tests (valid, missing, malformed ID) and document the extraction format for content teams.",
            "Map Vimeo videos to Squiz/CMS IDs using metadata placed in the Vimeo description field so video records can be joined with CMS data and indexed consistently.",
            "Measure latency impact of retrieval architecture changes to verify whether removing unnecessary Gremlin calls and restructuring reasoning improves response time.",
            "Move Gremlin tool-call execution into the reasoning node so it can call the Gremlin execution tool directly, receive execution errors and attempt self-correction, instead of handing off a query idea to a separate executing node; compare against the previous two-node architecture on answer quality and latency.",
            "Move Gremlin tool-call execution into the reasoning node so it can observe execution errors and self-correct instead of handing off only a query idea to another node.",
            "Move Gremlin tool-call execution into the reasoning node: the reasoning node calls the Gremlin execution tool directly and receives execution errors it can use to attempt correction, replacing the previous architecture where one node generated a query idea and another executed it; evaluation considers both answer quality and latency.",
            "Natural-language interface over approved pharmaceutical knowledge sources covering product information and characteristics, active substances, contraindications and adverse reactions, interactions (where data sources/integrations available), reimbursement information, medical articles and educational materials, clinical calculators via integration, and contextual eDetailing materials for selected Polpharma products. Every medical/product answer must be traceable to source material (source grounding as core trust mechanism). Azure-based deployment in Polpharma-provided cloud; modular, API-first, cloud-native architecture using managed Azure services; Graph RAG and hybrid retrieval. Governance emphasis: Responsible AI, AI Act awareness, auditability, human oversight, controlled knowledge grounding.",
            "Negatively rated production questions are to be added to the evaluation dataset so that future model and retrieval changes are tested against known failure cases.",
            "Organize retrieval-optimization work under a dedicated backlog epic covering dedicated tools, Gremlin fallback, AI Search replacement, buttons/clarifications, routing, latency, and evaluation; consolidate scattered stories and reflect the plan discussed in the workshop meeting rather than isolated technical changes.",
            "Organize retrieval-optimization work under a dedicated backlog epic so that stories around dedicated tools, latency, routing, AI Search, Graph retrieval, and clarification flows are managed as one coherent plan.",
            "Paraphrasing node should no longer produce narrative phrasing ('the user asks about...') as the primary search query; paraphrases should be short, content-focused, retrieval-suitable, and preserve medically relevant terms. Retrieval quality is evaluated against cases where vector search previously returned weak few-shot examples. Next: evaluate whether semantic search or ranking improves few-shot example retrieval for Gremlin-related prompting.",
            "Polish medical NLP: recognition of medicines, active substances, diseases, ICD-10 codes, adverse effects, contraindications and related pharmaceutical concepts; normalization of Polish medical terminology; handling of inflection and synonymy; intent classification into supported conversational flows; clarification of ambiguous or under-specified queries. eDetailing module acting as digital medical representative: detect mentions linked with promotional materials, track materials shown, respect frequency/visibility preferences, answer questions about displayed materials from indexed content, cite source fragments. Analytics layer: conversation topics and intents, failed/unresolved journeys, thumbs-up/down feedback and comments, source usage and retrieval path, risk flags for answer quality and compliance, potential adverse-event signals, LLM technical and cost telemetry - supporting continuous improvement, quality monitoring, content gap detection and prioritization of future development.",
            "Provide human-readable descriptions of important fields (including status/flag-style fields) to the answer-generation step, accompany returned data with context explaining field meanings, avoid presenting raw technical field values as user-facing medical explanations, and distinguish dose vs dosage questions so doctors get the correct type of information about drug strength or administration instructions.",
            "Record and report suspected Farmindex ICD-10 data quality issues to Polpharma without correcting source data; optimize list-style ICD-10 responses by generating a short introduction with a small model or predefined pattern and appending the retrieved product list directly (no full list passed to the main LLM), with Polish grammatical correctness and regression tests; implement a dedicated ATC retrieval tool for drug-group questions.",
            "Record for each answer whether it was grounded via Graph retrieval or AI Search, aggregate the metric to measure source usage frequency and evaluate whether Graph retrieval is justified; integrate ICD-10 data and map disease names/groups to ICD-10 codes for drug-recommendation scenarios.",
            "Replace Gremlin retrieval with AI Search for drug-property questions where Graph traversal is unnecessary, to reduce latency, complexity, and error risk.",
            "Review and improve the similar-question retrieval strategy: confirm whether it uses vector, keyword, hybrid search and/or reranking, document known quality concerns, propose improvement options such as hybrid search or semantic reranking, identify at least one weak scenario, and recommend whether to implement improvements now or defer; no production behavior changed unless separately approved.",
            "Review entity state before tool calls so it contains only entities relevant to the current question; remove or deprioritize irrelevant entities from previous turns while keeping still-relevant entities for follow-up questions; support dedicated tool calls relying on clean slot filling; ask a clarification question when a drug or condition cannot be confidently resolved instead of calling tools with the wrong entity.",
            "Review the current similar-question retrieval implementation: confirm whether it uses vector search, keyword search, hybrid search and/or reranking; document known quality concerns; propose improvement options such as hybrid search or semantic reranking; identify at least one representative failing or weak scenario; recommend whether to implement improvements now or keep as future optimization; no production behavior changed unless separately approved.",
            "Routing layer detects when the user asks about a drug property, determines which property or field is needed where possible, and invokes the AI Search-based drug-property retrieval tool for supported cases; routing design avoids excessively narrow low-level scenarios when a higher-level scenario is more manageable; question-paraphrasing node to generate concise system-oriented search queries so vector search retrieves more relevant examples without overweighting generic phrases such as 'the user asks about'.",
            "Run a controlled experiment comparing current (English) prompting against Polish-language prompting for selected medical retrieval scenarios, including scenarios where Polish reasoning was suspected to perform better; evaluate answer quality and token/cost implications; recommend whether to keep English prompts, move selected prompts to Polish, or use a mixed approach.",
            "Scenario coverage report showing how much historical traffic can be handled by AI Search versus Graph, to support evidence-based retrieval optimization decisions.",
            "Support multi-step retrieval decomposition: decompose selected complex questions into smaller retrieval operations, combine intermediate results using deterministic tools such as intersection, test on examples where one-shot Gremlin generation is fragile, and base the final answer on retrieved intermediate outputs rather than unsupported LLM inference.",
            "The fallback reasoning node returns a strict structured format instead of free-form prose, avoiding unnecessary explanatory text when only structured query-planning data is required; configured through prompting, output schema, token limits, or a combination; the new format is evaluated against examples where longer reasoning output correlated with poorer results.",
            "The flattened architecture experiment compares quality, latency, and controllability against the current structured approach; it is treated as exploratory and not as the default delivery architecture unless validated.",
            "Use AI Search instead of Graph/Gremlin for drug-property questions answerable from indexed SmPC/ChPL fields; pass retrieved context with source information to the answer-generation step; keep Graph retrieval for scenarios requiring structured traversal; goal is reduced latency, complexity and error risk.",
            "Use small specialized tools (e.g. a list intersection tool accepting two or more retrieved result lists and returning their intersection) and decompose complex medical questions into smaller retrieval steps that can be tested and combined, instead of forcing the LLM to solve everything in one large Gremlin query.",
            "Use small specialized tools (e.g., a deterministic list-intersection tool combining two or more retrieved result lists) instead of forcing the LLM to solve everything in one query; support multi-step questions combining constraints.",
            "Using the authorized doctor's location context, the system should indicate whether and where a drug is available to the patient; when a drug is unavailable it should suggest alternative drugs currently available in pharmacies and wholesalers; for reimbursed drugs it should display reimbursement information and rules and provide a ready, NFZ-compliant reimbursement justification template to paste; for drugs with parameter-dependent dosing it should give access to dose calculators, link to the relevant calculator when presenting results, and in dialogue collect required input parameters, ask for missing ones and return the computed dose.",
            "Videos without transcripts are skipped during indexing so that incomplete Vimeo uploads do not create broken or low-quality searchable records.",
            "WAP-generated article links include configurable analytics query parameters so Polpharma's existing web analytics system can attribute article clicks originating from the assistant." ;
