        rdf:object "Paraphrasing node should no longer produce narrative phrasing ('the user asks about...') as the primary search query; paraphrases should be short, content-focused, retrieval-suitable, and preserve medically relevant terms. Retrieval quality is evaluated against cases where vector search previously returned weak few-shot examples. Next: evaluate whether semantic search or ranking improves few-shot example retrieval for Gremlin-related prompting." ;
        rdf:predicate fact:solution-direction ;
        rdf:subject entity:pharma-assistant ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/text-ontology/document/doc-28b154549e870b67> .

